* G1_TOP breaker path, chip level: held45mV fault40us, HOLD_TIME=0 means8192cycles, one automaticretry then giveup; serialSTATUS/STATUS2/TRIP_CNT
* case retry_read | block netlists pex | front end beh | clock to the RTL ideal | corner tt (mos_tt res_typ cap_typ hbt_typ) | 27 degC | run_top.py
.param VDDA=3.3 VDD=1.2 IOVDD=3.3 RSH=25m RGND=10m INOM=1 CVREF=1e-08
.lib /foss/pdks/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOSlv.lib mos_tt
.lib /foss/pdks/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib mos_tt
.lib /foss/pdks/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib res_typ
.lib /foss/pdks/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerCAP.lib cap_typ
.lib /foss/pdks/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerHBT.lib hbt_typ
.lib /foss/pdks/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerDIO.lib dio_tt
.include /foss/pdks/ihp-sg13g2/libs.ref/sg13g2_io/spice/sg13g2_io.spi
.include /work/designs/g1-guardian/blocks/g1_gate/sim/postlayout/g1_gate_pex.spice
.temp 27
.global sub!
Vsub sub! 0 dc 0
* solver (README, "Numerical notes"): gear integration and loose absolute tolerances are what the PDK IO-pad
* models need when XSPICE events fall on their switching edges (with abstol 1e-9 / vntol 1e-5 the diode
* internal nodes stop converging: "timestep too small"); the DAC mux-tree nodes need rshunt; XSPICE forces
* trtol = 1, which the comparator decisions need at this reltol; default gmin (1e-13 stalls the pads)
.option method=gear itl4=100 reltol=0.002 abstol=1e-8 vntol=1e-4 chgtol=1e-12 rshunt=1e12
* ---- supplies: one 3.3 V board rail feeds VDDA (pin 7) and IOVDD (pin 3), PLAN D14; 1.2 V VDD (pin 1)
V33 rail33 0 dc 3.3
Vma rail33 vdda_s dc 0
Vmi rail33 iovdd_s dc 0
Rsa vdda_s vdda 0.5
Cda vdda 0 1n
Rsi iovdd_s iovdd 0.5
Cdi iovdd 0 1n
V12 vdd_s 0 dc 1.2
Rsd vdd_s vdd 0.5
Cdd vdd 0 1n
* ---- board: load current profile (1 V = 1 A) x switch on the FET gate node, shunt, Kelvin traces, FET gate
Vprof iprof 0 pwl(0 1 4e-05 1 4.002e-05 1.8)
Bload 0 ldi I = v(iprof) * (0.5 + 0.5*tanh((v(gfet) - 1.5)/0.15))
Vim ldi shp dc 0
Rsh shp shn {RSH}
Rgnd shn 0 {RGND}
Rkp shp sense_p 1
Rkn shn sense_n 1
Rg gate gfet 10
Cgate gfet 0 5n
Cfault fault_n 0 20p
* ---- pads (PDK sg13g2_io SPICE models): SENSE_P/N on the bare pad terminal, VREF on the padres terminal
* (587 Ohm secondary protection, padframe/README.md); the VREF bond pad carries the board capacitor CVREF
XPSP sense_p sense_p_res vdd 0 iovdd 0 sg13g2_IOPadAnalog
XPSN sense_n sense_n_res vdd 0 iovdd 0 sg13g2_IOPadAnalog
XPVREF vref_pad vref vdd 0 iovdd 0 sg13g2_IOPadAnalog
Cvref_ext vref_pad 0 {CVREF}
* digital input pads (EN, SCLK, SDI) as ideal 3.3 V -> 1.2 V level copies: the sg13g2_IOPadIn SPICE
* models abort the event-driven solver at their input edges with the charge tolerance the comparators
* need (README, "Numerical notes"); the pads are functionally verified in blocks/g1_gate (EN pad)
Ben_core en_core 0 V = v(en_pad)*1.2/3.3
Bsclk_core sclk_core 0 V = v(sclk_pad)*1.2/3.3
Bsdi_core sdi_core 0 V = v(sdi_pad)*1.2/3.3
* GATE / FAULT_N output pads as behavioural drivers fitted to the g1_gate block results with the PDK pad
* models (30 mA pad: 5 nF + 10 Ohm, fall 90-10 % 606 ns, arming 0-90 % 677 ns -> 47 Ohm driver; 4 mA pad:
* 20 pF, ~500 Ohm). Reason: README, "Numerical notes" (pad models and the StrongARM comparators need
* incompatible integration settings). The driver switches within 1 ns of gate_core / fault_core and
* draws its current from IOVDD.
Bgate_drv gate_drv 0 V = v(iovdd)*(0.5 + 0.5*tanh((v(gate_core) - 0.6)/0.05))
Rgate_drv gate_drv gate 47
Bgate_i iovdd 0 I = max(0, (v(gate_drv) - v(gate))/47)
Bfault_drv fault_drv 0 V = v(iovdd)*(0.5 + 0.5*tanh((v(fault_core) - 0.6)/0.05))
Rfault_drv fault_drv fault_n 500
Ven en_pad 0 pwl(0 0 3.04640871692e-06 0 3.04730871692e-06 1.485 3.04750871692e-06 1.815 3.04840871692e-06 3.3)
